    {
      "id": "2124033377208865278",
      "text": "RT @kcoleman: @aakashgupta This is not accurate: \"one report erases 468 likes.\" That's not what the code is doing. The weights are a multip…",
      "created_at": "Sat Nov 21 06:53:14 +0000 2026",
      "lang": "en",
      "media": [],
      "retweet": {
        "id": "2088005608415133767",
        "text": "This is not accurate: \"one report erases 468 likes.\" That's not what the code is doing. The weights are a multiple on your own predicted probability of Liking, Reporting, etc, which is substantially driven by your own behavior. And the baseline probability of a Report is more than 1000x lower. \n\nAlso: https://t.co/VSjloVHjXG",
        "created_at": "Thu Aug 13 20:51:44 +0000 2026",
        "lang": "en",
        "media": [],
        "retweet": null,
        "quoted": {
          "id": "2087992223648682249",
          "text": "@AutismCapital @IterIntellectus It is not possible to game -- since the action has to take place on a post served in Home Timeline. Directly navigating to a post (i.e., coordinating via groupchat) has no ranking impact. \n\nAnd users cannot manufacture a post to show up in their Timeline in any reproducible way.",
          "created_at": "Thu Aug 13 19:58:33 +0000 2026",
          "lang": "en",
          "media": [],
          "retweet": null,
          "quoted": null,
          "user": {
